From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 20:34:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ios: the player's arrangement of the touch controls
 (DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT)

Players want to move the touch controls themselves (LNPANDY/NX2Apple#414,
#347, seedds/nxnative#740). The earlier editor (patch 0036, reverted in
#345) scattered the controls and broke the layout on a multi-game
install. This one is safe by construction.

DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT is one value, written by a front end's layout editor:
"1", then per layout ";", its name and "/control:dx,dy" for each moved
control, for example 1;2d/face:0,-2/stick:1,-1;3d/a:-1,0. There is one
arrangement each for 2D, 3D and both again for the split screen (2s, 3s:
DmLayout.separated, an iPad upright and iPhone Duo upright or half open).
The controls are the diamond as a whole (face) and each of its keys (a b x
y, from where the diamond is), the left stick, the D-pad, ZL L ZR R, L3
R3, minus and plus. The menu button stays, and a moved control keeps
out of its hit circle. Offsets are steps of a
quarter of a face key's width at the player's size, so a layout scales
with the controls and not with the screen. The engine stores nothing.

The geometry (DmPadGeometry.h) applies it after the size and the left
stick's place. Each moved control is pushed back inside the area its
built-in place uses (the safe area, the bottom corners halfway into the
side insets as always) and placed only if it stays 10 u (at least 10
points) clear of every other drawn control. Otherwise it keeps its
built-in place. The diamond goes first, then its single keys. Each round
places what fits and tries the rest again, so a control can take a place
another one has left. Whatever the value, the result is a layout with
every control inside and none on another. An unknown layout or control
is skipped. Any other malformed value, or one longer than 1024
characters, is ignored whole. The log says when a value is ignored and
which moved controls kept their place.

The touch-down decision moves out of DmGamepad.m into dm_pad_hit and
dm_pad_menu_takes (the menu button), pure functions of the same
geometry, so drawing, hit-test and grab cannot
disagree. Without an arrangement it decides exactly as before. With one,
the locked keys go to the nearest, and a diamond whose keys were moved
one by one is grabbed key by key.

test_pad_geometry.py: a value of zeros gives the built-in layout exactly
on every screen, the value's form (malformed and too-long values ignored,
unknown names skipped, random bytes), and seeded random arrangements on
every screen, layout, size and stick place: every control inside its
area and on the screen, no two overlapping, a moved one clear by the gap,
and a touch inside any drawn control taken by that control.

Upstream-Status: pending (builds on seedds/nxnative#683, which landed as e2fadf22)
Reason: Players arrange the touch controls themselves (#414, #347)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#414
